---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Output formats" current="/reference/output/">
  <article class="doc">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Reference</span>
      <h1>Output formats</h1>
      <p class="lead">Use text output locally, JSON for scripts, and SARIF for code scanning systems.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>Text</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint found 2 issues in 1 file after 47ms

settings.json
  /name   type      expected string, received number
  /count  minimum   must be >= 1

Summary: 4 discovered, 3 validated, 1 skipped, 2 issues in 47ms</code></pre>

    <h2>Text with locations</h2>
    <pre><code>settings.json
  3:11  type      expected string, received number  /name
  4:12  minimum   must be >= 1   /count</code></pre>

    <h2>JSON</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint validate . --json</code></pre>
    <p>JSON output includes the run root, summary counts, per-file results, issues, warnings, schema locations, and optional source positions.</p>

    <h2>SARIF</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint validate . --sarif &gt; dollarlint.sarif</code></pre>
    <p>SARIF output targets GitHub code scanning and similar tools. Source locations are best-effort and fall back to the nearest file or parent object when a precise range is not available.</p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
